        'title'=>$title,
        'subtitle'=>'Use place-value ideas and visual models to '.$focus.'.',
        'essential_question'=>'How can place value and a clear model help us '.$focus.'?',
        'learning_targets'=>"I can name the value of each digit.\nI can choose a place-value model or strategy that fits the problem.\nI can solve and check my answer.",
        'vocabulary'=>str_replace('; ',"\n",$item['vocab']),
        'worked_examples'=>$item['example'],
        'common_mistakes'=>"Reading a digit without naming its place | Say both the digit and its value.\nMisaligning places | Line up equal place values, especially decimal points.\nRegrouping without explaining the trade | State which 10 smaller units become 1 larger unit.\nSkipping a reasonableness check | Estimate before or after calculating.",
        'real_life'=>'Base-ten reasoning helps us read prices, measure distances, compare populations, estimate costs, and calculate accurately with whole numbers and decimals.',
        'videos'=>$title.' | https://www.khanacademy.org/math/cc-'.(stripos($grade,'Kindergarten')!==false?'kindergarten':strtolower(str_replace(' ','-',$grade))).'-math',
        'video_chapters'=>"0:00 | Read the number or problem\n1:00 | Build the place-value model\n2:15 | Choose a strategy\n3:30 | Solve and check",
        'practice_warmup'=>$practice($item['warm'],'Use a quick place-value model. Label what each digit or quantity means.'),
        'guided_practice'=>$practice($item['guided'],'Follow each step. Build or draw the model, write the calculation, and explain each place-value move.'),
        'independent_practice'=>$practice($item['independent'],'Choose a model or algorithm, show your work, and enter your final answer.'),
        'challenge_practice'=>$item['challenge'],
        'master_it'=>"I can explain the value of a digit using correct vocabulary.\nI can use a model and an efficient calculation strategy.\nI can check whether my answer is reasonable.",
        'mastery_questions'=>"Why must digits be aligned when adding? | To make the writing pretty ; To combine equal place values ; To make every number longer ; To avoid regrouping | B\nWhat does regrouping mean? | Rename equal value using different place-value units ; Change the answer ; Round every number ; Move the decimal randomly | A\nWhich check is useful after calculating? | Estimate the expected size ; Ignore the units ; Change an addend ; Read only the last digit | A\nA digit one place to the left is how many times the value? | 2 ; 5 ; 10 ; 100 | C\nWhy use a visual model? | It shows the place-value relationship ; It removes all numbers ; It gives every answer ; It replaces explaining | A",
        'parent_summary'=>'Students use objects, drawings, number lines, place-value charts, and algorithms to understand how our base-ten number system works. Explanations and estimation are emphasized along with accuracy.',
        'parent_conversation'=>"Ask: What is the value of each digit?\nAsk: What trade or regrouping happened?\nAsk: What estimate tells you the answer makes sense?",
        'parent_five_minute'=>'Choose a number from a receipt, address, or measurement. Ask your child to read it, write it in expanded form, compare it with another number, and explain the value of one digit.',
        'teacher_objectives'=>"Students will represent numbers and operations with grade-appropriate base-ten models.\nStudents will calculate accurately with place-value reasoning.\nStudents will explain and check their strategy using precise vocabulary.",
        'teacher_pacing'=>"Launch | 5 minutes | Connect to a familiar number or measurement.\nLearn It | 10 minutes | Model the place-value relationship visually.\nWorked Example | 8 minutes | Explain each place-value decision.\nGuided Practice | 12 minutes | Release one step at a time.\nIndependent Practice | 12 minutes | Require a model or labeled algorithm.\nMastery | 5 minutes | Check accuracy, vocabulary, and reasoning.",
        'teacher_misconceptions'=>"Students name the digit instead of its value | Ask for the digit, place, and value separately.\nStudents compare by number length or last digit | Compare from the greatest place first.\nStudents regroup procedurally without understanding | Model every trade with base-ten units.\nStudents misalign decimals | Use a place-value chart and equivalent trailing zeros.",
        'teacher_differentiation'=>"Beginning | Use concrete base-ten blocks and smaller numbers.\nDeveloping | Connect blocks to drawings and expanded form.\nOn Level | Move among models, algorithms, and explanations.\nAdvanced | Compare methods and justify general place-value rules.\nMultilingual Learners | Pair vocabulary with labeled visual models and sentence frames.",
        'teacher_formative'=>"Ask students to identify a digit, its place, and its value.\nCheck whether the visual model matches the written number or calculation.\nListen for an explanation of every regrouping.\nUse an estimate and one transfer problem as an exit check.",
        'standards'=>'CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.'.$item['standard'].' — '.$grade.' Number & Operations in Base Ten.\nStandards for Mathematical Practice: SMP 1, SMP 2, SMP 3, SMP 4, SMP 6, and SMP 7.'
    ];
};

return array_map($expand,$lessons);
